From 73a16f246dd8d239d54485d29bb3fc0cbf8ea09e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:04:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the simplified rounding under the GUI only
 where its frames do not keep up

CDVStepDown leaves the frames with GUI elements out of its measurements, so a
profile 5 picture whose frames fit without the GUI and miss refreshes with the
player information open is never helped: on the integrated Radeon of a Ryzen 9
7950X3D, up to 52 ms a frame on average over 10 s, and 56 at most, of a
41.7 ms film refresh, where the frames without GUI elements, and those of
profile 7 FEL and 8.1 with it, fit.

CDVGuiRound decides, for each picture format, fidelity step-down level and
refresh period, whether the frames with GUI elements of a profile 5 picture ask
the bridge for the simplified rounding under the GUI
(dvbridge_render_simplify_gui()). It goes on only after those frames are
measured behind with the rule of CDVStepDown: GPU time over its mark and
missed refreshes, in two windows of 48 frames in a row, or in one where they
take more than the period; nothing while frames can still be presented a frame
ahead, which comes first. The first seconds of a video and after a seek, and
the first second after GUI elements come, are left out. It goes off when the
exact rounding would take no more than the release mark of CDVStepDown, by the
ratio of the two measured when it went on, and not before a minute of film of
those frames; each time it has to go on again after going off, that wait
doubles.

Only where Kodi chooses the fidelity (the settings of the step-down), only for
frames with GUI elements (not subtitles alone, nor a capture), and the bridge
draws it only for profile 5 in the source transport: frames without GUI
elements, profile 7 FEL and 8.1 never change, and a GPU whose frames with GUI
elements keep up never turns it on. A line in the log when it goes on or off
for a format; while the frames are drawn that way, the fidelity step-down row
of the Dolby Vision page and of the summary says so (hades.dv.guiround, string
31873, in en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx).

The decision has a host test (both ways, 26 checks) and 15 mutations of it,
all caught.
